/* book Worked example: Q: A single lap joint uses 4 rivets of 4 mm diameter. The allowable shear stress of the rivet material is 200 MPa. Find the load the joint can carry in rivet shear if all four rivets share it equally.
   1. Rivet diameter d = 4 mm = 0.004 m. Area A = π d²/4 = π × 0.004² ÷ 4 = 1.257 × 10⁻⁵ m² (12.57 mm²).
   2. Allowable shear stress τ = 200 MPa = 200 × 10⁶ N/m². Load per rivet F₁ = τ A = 200 × 10⁶ × 1.257 × 10⁻⁵ = 2513 N.
   3. Four rivets share equally: total F = 4 × 2513 = 10 053 N.
   Answer: In rivet shear the joint carries about 10 053 N, or 10.1 kN, with ideal equal sharing; bearing, net section and the eccentricity of a single lap must still be checked. */
