/* book Worked example 2: Q: Two 2024-T3 sheets, each 2 mm thick and 60 mm wide, are joined in a single lap by one row of 3 rivets of 5 mm diameter across the width. Allowables: rivet shear 180 MPa, sheet bearing 500 MPa, sheet net-section tension 300 MPa. Find the strength of the joint, the mode that governs, and the joint efficiency against the uncut sheet.
   1. Rivet shear: P = n τ πd²/4 = 3 × 180 × 10⁶ × π × 0.005² ÷ 4 = 3 × 180 × 10⁶ × 1.9635 × 10⁻⁵ = 10 603 N.
   2. Bearing: P = n d t σbr = 3 × 0.005 × 0.002 × 500 × 10⁶ = 15 000 N.
   3. Net section: three holes remove 3 × 5 = 15 mm of the 60 mm width, so the net width is 45 mm. P = 0.045 × 0.002 × 300 × 10⁶ = 27 000 N.
   4. The smallest value governs: rivet shear, 10 603 N.
   5. Uncut sheet strength = 0.060 × 0.002 × 300 × 10⁶ = 36 000 N. Efficiency = 10 603 ÷ 36 000 = 0.295, about 29 %.
   Answer:  */
